## Context
Child of tracker 1254. Cause isolated on 2026-10-27 (see 1254's log): two pytest-xdist workers can
draw the same loopback port from `tests/zotero_live.py::free_port()`; the second Zotero starts
without a bind error and the fixture's readiness checks pass against the other worker's server,
so keyed writes fail with HTTP 401. Reproduced deterministically by forcing both `LiveZotero`
instances onto one port.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `LiveZotero` detects a foreign listener on its port at startup (one keyed write, 401 means
      foreign; or the LISTEN socket's owner is not the fixture's process group), stops its client,
      draws a new port and retries a bounded number of times.
- [ ] A test forces two fixtures onto one port and shows the second retries and both write; the
      same test fails on the code before the fix.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.

## Relevant files
tests/zotero_live.py, tests/test_zotero_import.py

Related: [[1254]], [[1258]].
